&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Traverse Theatre&lt;br /&gt;
	10 Cambridge Street&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Traverse is Scotland's 'new writing theatre' and showcases work from playwrights, new and established, in it's pair of purpose-built theatre spaces.&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;iframe frameborder=&quot;0&quot; height=&quot;350&quot; marginheight=&quot;0&quot; marginwidth=&quot;0&quot; scrolling=&quot;no&quot; src=&quot;http://maps.google.co.uk/maps?f=q&amp;source=s_q&amp;hl=en&amp;geocode=&amp;q=Traverse+Theatre,+Cambridge+Street,+Edinburgh&amp;aq=0&amp;oq=traverse+theatre,+Edinburgh&amp;sll=55.947241,-3.205411&amp;sspn=0.002854,0.005955&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;hq=Traverse+Theatre,+Cambridge+Street,+Edinburgh&amp;ll=55.94759,-3.204746&amp;spn=0.012496,0.032015&amp;t=m&amp;output=embed&iwloc=near&quot; width=&quot;400&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Lothian Buses&lt;/b&gt;: 1, 10, 11, 15, 15A, 16, 24, 34&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Parking:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;br /&gt;
	There are a limited number of disabled badge spaces on Grindlay Street and Cambridge Street.&nbsp;NCP car park&nbsp;on Castle Terrace.&lt;br /&gt;
	&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Access:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Level access&nbsp;Box Office from&nbsp;Cambridge Street.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		There is a lift with Braille signage and an audible announcer.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Wheelchair spaces are available.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Lift with voice announcement and Braille buttons to all levels. For lift access to Traverse 1, please make yourself known to a member of the Front of House team.&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Accessible toilets at ground and lower ground&nbsp;Bar Caf&Atilde;&copy; levels.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Infrared hearing enhancement system. Headsets available from staff.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Wheelchair spaces available.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

