&lt;p align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ross Theatre and Princes Street Gardens&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Virgin Money Fireworks Concert&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;iframe frameborder=&quot;0&quot; height=&quot;350&quot; marginheight=&quot;0&quot; marginwidth=&quot;0&quot; scrolling=&quot;no&quot; src=&quot;http://maps.google.co.uk/maps?f=q&amp;source=s_q&amp;hl=en&amp;geocode=&amp;q=Ross+Theatre,+Edinburgh&amp;aq=0&amp;oq=ross+theatre,+Edinburgh&amp;sll=55.94759,-3.204746&amp;sspn=0.002854,0.005955&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;hq=Ross+Theatre,&amp;hnear=Edinburgh,+Midlothian,+United+Kingdom&amp;ll=55.952288,-3.193317&amp;spn=0.006295,0.01111&amp;t=m&amp;output=embed&iwloc=near&quot; width=&quot;400&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
	&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sunday&nbsp;2 September 9.00pm&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Parking:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		&lt;div&gt;
			Please visit &lt;a href=&quot;/virginmoneyfireworks&quot;&gt;eif.co.uk/virginmoneyfireworks &lt;/a&gt;for most up-to-date information on transport and parking advice for the Virgin Money Fireworks Concert.&lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Access:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Level access to the Gardens and Ross Theatre approximately 200 metres from the King's Stables Road entrance. Please arrive before 8.00pm.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Wheelchair spaces available in the Ross Theatre and Princes Street Gardens, please tell the box office if you would like to use either of these areas when you book your tickets.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Accessible toilets located in the gardens and behind the Ross Theatre.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Please note that the gardens become very crowded and combined with the noisy fireworks may make this event unsuitable for assistance animals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Call 0131 473 2089 if you have any further questions about the Ross Theatre and Princes Street Gardens.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Festival Theatre, Edinburgh&lt;br /&gt;
	13-29 Nicolson Street&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;br /&gt;
	The Festival Theatre has 1915 seats making it the second largest theatre in Edinburgh. Built on the site of the Empire Theatre, the auditorium has been restored to its former glory and with its large stage, is ideal for large scale dance and opera productions. The Theatre's striking glass frontage provides a dramatic entrance to the traditional art deco auditorium.&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;iframe frameborder=&quot;0&quot; height=&quot;350&quot; marginheight=&quot;0&quot; marginwidth=&quot;0&quot; scrolling=&quot;no&quot; src=&quot;http://maps.google.co.uk/maps?f=q&amp;source=s_q&amp;hl=en&amp;geocode=&amp;q=Festival+Theatre+Edinburgh,+Nicolson+Street,+Edinburgh&amp;aq=0&amp;oq=festival+theatre+edinburgh&amp;sll=55.944083,-3.161833&amp;sspn=0.034751,0.062571&amp;g=Arthur%27s+Seat&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;hq=Festival+Theatre+Edinburgh,+Nicolson+Street,+Edinburgh&amp;ll=55.94684,-3.186202&amp;spn=0.004344,0.007821&amp;t=m&amp;z=14&amp;iwloc=A&amp;cid=26498133126844169&amp;output=embed&iwloc=near&quot; width=&quot;425&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;strong&gt;Lothian Buses: &lt;/strong&gt;3, 3A, 5, 7, 8, 14, 29, 30, 31, 33, 37, 47, X47, 49&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;strong&gt;Access Information:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Single yellow lines and Pay and Display spaces on side streets.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		There is a pavement ramp, or six steps with one handrail, at the front of theatre.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Level access is available at a side entrance.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		There is lift access to all levels of the theatre which has a voice announcement.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Wheelchair spaces in stalls on floor 1.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Sennheiser infrared system is available in all areas of the auditorium. Receivers for use either with or without a hearing aid are available, headsets can be collected from the cloakroom on the mezzanine.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Accessible toilets on levels 1 and 2 of the theatre.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Cafe/bar on ground floor with lift access to other bars.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		There is Braille and tactile signage throughout the building.&lt;br /&gt;
		&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Call 0131 473 2089 if you have any further questions about the Festival Theatre, Edinburgh.&lt;/p&gt;

