&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Greyfriars Kirk&lt;br /&gt;
	Greyfriars Place&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;br /&gt;
	Located at the top of Candlemaker Row, and less than ten minutes walk from the Royal Mile, the Kirk is the perfect place to hear an early evening concert.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;iframe frameborder=&quot;0&quot; height=&quot;350&quot; marginheight=&quot;0&quot; marginwidth=&quot;0&quot; scrolling=&quot;no&quot; src=&quot;http://maps.google.co.uk/maps?f=q&amp;source=s_q&amp;hl=en&amp;geocode=&amp;q=Greyfriars+Kirk,+Candlemaker+Row,+Edinburgh&amp;aq=1&amp;oq=Greyfriars+kir,+Edinburgh&amp;sll=55.947085,-3.186207&amp;sspn=0.004344,0.007821&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;hq=Greyfriars+Kirk,+Candlemaker+Row,+Edinburgh&amp;t=m&amp;ll=55.946629,-3.192301&amp;spn=0.012496,0.032015&amp;output=embed&quot; width=&quot;425&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lothian Buses: &lt;/strong&gt;2, 23, 27, 41, 42, 67&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Parking:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Pay and display on Chambers Street, oppostie the Kirk. Parking is not permitted in the Kirkyard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Access:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		&lt;div&gt;
			Level access to the Kirk.&lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Wheelchair spaces available in the Kirk and an accessible toilet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Call 0131 473 2089 if you have any further questions about Greyfriars Kirk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Queen's Hall&lt;br /&gt;
	85 - 89 Clerk Street&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Queen's Hall is a 900 seat concert hall located on the southside of Edinburgh just 15-20 minutes walk from Princes Street, and 10-15 minutes from the Royal Mile. Previously a church, this lovely Georgian building is the perfect setting for an intimate series of Festival morning recitals.&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;br /&gt;
	A cafe bar is located on the ground floor of the Hall, selling tea, coffee, soft drinks and alcoholic beverages. The box office is located next door to the main building and will be selling tickets for all International Festival performances from Monday 26 March.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;iframe frameborder=&quot;0&quot; height=&quot;350&quot; marginheight=&quot;0&quot; marginwidth=&quot;0&quot; scrolling=&quot;no&quot; src=&quot;http://maps.google.co.uk/maps?f=q&amp;source=s_q&amp;hl=en&amp;geocode=&amp;q=The+Queen%27s+Hall,+Clerk+Street,+Newington,+Edinburgh&amp;aq=0&amp;oq=queen%27s+hall,+edinburgh&amp;sll=53.800651,-4.064941&amp;sspn=24.810233,48.779297&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;hq=The+Queen%27s+Hall,+Clerk+Street,+Newington,+Edinburgh&amp;ll=55.941248,-3.181425&amp;spn=0.012498,0.032015&amp;t=m&amp;output=embed&iwloc=near&quot; width=&quot;400&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lothian Buses: &lt;/strong&gt;3, 3A, 5, 7, 8, 14, 29, 30, 31, 33, 37, 47, X47,&nbsp;49&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Access information:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Single yellow line parking on side streets.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Ramped access to double door with automatic door opener.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Wheelchair spaces on the ground floor at the centre and sides of the Hall. The gallery is accessible by stairs only.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Induction loop in stalls and Sennheiser infrared system is available throughout the auditorium.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Receivers for use both with and without a hearing aid are available from the cloakroom.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		There is a unisex accessible toilet on the ground floor with level access and handrails.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Cafe/bar on ground floor.&lt;br /&gt;
		&lt;br /&gt;
		Please call 0131 473 2089 if you have any further questions about The Queen's Hall.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Hub&lt;br /&gt;
	Castlehill, Royal Mile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;br /&gt;
	The Hub is a magnificent Gothic building situated at the top of the Royal Mile. It is operated by Edinburgh Festival Centre Ltd, a wholly owned subsidiary of the Edinburgh International Festival Society, and is a popular visitor attraction in its own right, welcoming over 500,000 visitors a year. The tip of its spire is the highest point in central Edinburgh, visible for miles around.&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;br /&gt;
	The Hub is open all year round, and houses its own restaurant, Cafe Hub; a spectacular Main Hall, which is a popular venue for concerts, ceilidhs, banquets and parties; and two smaller venues, the Dunard Library and the Glass Room, used for meetings and more intimate parties. All of these areas are available for commercial hire. You will also find Hub Tickets here, the central box office for the Edinburgh International Festival and a range of other events throughout the year.&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;br /&gt;
	In August the Hub is a busy Festival venue hosting several International Festival events including music, theatre and Festival Insights.&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;iframe frameborder=&quot;0&quot; height=&quot;350&quot; marginheight=&quot;0&quot; marginwidth=&quot;0&quot; scrolling=&quot;no&quot; src=&quot;http://maps.google.co.uk/maps?f=q&amp;source=s_q&amp;hl=en&amp;geocode=&amp;q=The+Hub,+Castlehill,+Edinburgh&amp;aq=0&amp;oq=The+Hub,+Cast&amp;sll=53.800651,-4.064941&amp;sspn=21.0873,39.506836&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;hq=The+Hub,+Castlehill,+Edinburgh&amp;ll=55.948778,-3.195986&amp;spn=0.012495,0.032015&amp;t=m&amp;output=embed&iwloc=near&quot; width=&quot;425&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
	To find out more about The Hub's banqueting and event facitilites, see the latest menus at Cafe Hub, or to take a virtual tour of the building, please visit &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.thehub-edinburgh.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; title=&quot;The Hub web site&quot;&gt;The Hub web site&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lothian Buses: &lt;/strong&gt;23, 27, 41, 42, 67 stop on George IV Bridge, 5 minutes from The Hub&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;strong&gt;Access:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Please contact The Hub on 0131 473 2089 for advice about parking during the Tattoo (3-25 August)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Level, ramped or lift access to all public areas.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Wheelchair spaces in the Main Hall.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Induction loop in Hub Tickets and the Main Hall.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Accessible toilet on ground floor and another via stair lift.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Bar and cafe on ground floor.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Lift with voice announcement and Braille buttons.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;br /&gt;
	Call 0131 473 2089 if you have any further questions about The Hub.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;The Usher Hall&lt;br /&gt;
	Lothian Road&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Usher Hall is one of the world's outstanding concert halls. A landmark in the heart of Edinburgh, it has hosted some of the greatest concerts and events in the city for a century.&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;iframe frameborder=&quot;0&quot; height=&quot;350&quot; marginheight=&quot;0&quot; marginwidth=&quot;0&quot; scrolling=&quot;no&quot; src=&quot;http://maps.google.co.uk/maps?f=q&amp;source=s_q&amp;hl=en&amp;geocode=&amp;q=Usher+Hall,+Lothian+Road,+Edinburgh&amp;aq=0&amp;oq=usher+hall,+Edinburgh&amp;sll=55.941248,-3.181427&amp;sspn=0.001427,0.002977&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;hq=Usher+Hall,+Lothian+Road,+Edinburgh&amp;t=m&amp;ll=55.947241,-3.205411&amp;spn=0.002854,0.005955&amp;output=embed&iwloc=near&quot; width=&quot;400&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Lothian Buses: &lt;/b&gt;1, 10, 11, 15, 15A, 16, 24, 34&lt;br /&gt;
	&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Access&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Limited number of disabled badge spaces on Grindlay Street and Cambridge Street. NCP car park on Castle Terrace.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Level access from Grindlay Street.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Lift access to all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Wheelchair spaces in the stalls and the grand circle.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Accessible toilets at stalls and grand circle levels.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Stalls cafe/bar fully accessible, upper circle bar accessible by lift.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Call 0131 473 2089 if you have any further questions about The Usher Hall.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dance Base&lt;br /&gt;
	14-16 Grassmarket&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dance Base is Scotland's National Centre for Dance, situated in a state of the art, custom designed building on the Grassmarket in the city's Old Town. It offers a vibrant and uplifting focal point which reaches out and inspires well-being and creativity and cultivates a future for dance in local, national and international communities.&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;iframe frameborder=&quot;0&quot; height=&quot;350&quot; marginheight=&quot;0&quot; marginwidth=&quot;0&quot; scrolling=&quot;no&quot; src=&quot;http://maps.google.co.uk/maps?f=q&amp;source=s_q&amp;hl=en&amp;geocode=&amp;q=dance+base,+Edinburgh&amp;aq=&amp;sll=55.94205,-3.202922&amp;sspn=0.005708,0.011909&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;hq=dance+base,&amp;hnear=Edinburgh,+Midlothian,+United+Kingdom&amp;t=m&amp;ll=55.94738,-3.197276&amp;spn=0.002854,0.005955&amp;z=14&amp;iwloc=A&amp;cid=1148423645437765056&amp;output=embed&quot; width=&quot;425&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;strong&gt;Lothian Buses: &lt;/strong&gt;23, 27, 41, 42, 67 stop on George IV Bridge, 5 minutes from Dance Base&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;br /&gt;
	&lt;strong&gt;Access Information:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		There is an NCP car park on Kings Stables Road, 10 minutes from Dance Base.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Level access.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Lift to all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Accessible toilet on floor 1 next to reception and upper foyer by main changing area&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
		Induction loop available.&lt;br /&gt;
		&lt;br /&gt;
		Call 0131 225 5525 if you have any further questions about Dance Base.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

